    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier start (81.88). Despite a 31% rain risk, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start due to his massive power-speed profile and a favorable matchup against Keider Montero. **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.66) also emerges as an elite option today; he benefits significantly from a dynamic platoon edge against the left-handed Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, allowing him to capitalize on his high-upside profile. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.61) provides unexpected value at 2B. Though he is projected to hit in the 8th spot, he is facing Max Scherzer, whose current 5.89 xERA makes him a primary target for our bats. This combination of a high-difficulty opposing arm and a strong platoon advantage elevates **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** into a rare tier for an 8-hole hitter.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the final bench spots, specifically keeping **Wade Meckler** (47.50) in the lineup over **Curtis Mead** (53.86). While **Curtis Mead** carries a higher efficiency score, the optimizer favored **Wade Meckler** to balance our lineup requirements and prioritize specific categorical coverage. **Curtis Mead** fell just short due to the projected lineup constraints and a slightly tougher park environment than initially modeled. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the status of **Sam Antonacci** (48.72); while his leadoff position provides a floor, he faces a difficult assignment in Max Fried, leaving his production as a marginal outcome we are tracking closely. We advise caution with all \"Lineup Pending\" designations, particularly regarding **Drake Baldwin** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, as any shift from their projected spots could necessitate a recalibration of our expected offensive output.",
